WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.960
So, how do we begin to dismantle rigidity and embrace emotional agility?

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:13.340
As that young schoolgirl, when I leaned into those blank pages, I started to do away with

3
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:20.680
feelings of what I should be experiencing, and instead started to open my heart to what

4
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:31.400
I did feel pain and grief and loss and regret.

5
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:38.040
Research now shows that the radical acceptance of all of our emotions, even the messy difficult

6
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:46.480
ones, is the cornerstone to resilience, thriving and true authentic happiness.

7
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.320
And emotional agility is more than just an acceptance of emotions.

8
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.400
We also know that accuracy matters.

9
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.920
In my own research, I've found that words are essential.

10
00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.840
We often use quick and easy labels to describe our feelings.

11
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.600
I'm stressed as the most common one I hear.

12
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.800
But there's a world of difference between stress and disappointment or stress and that

13
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.980
knowing dread of I'm in the wrong career.

14
00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:17.020
When we label our emotions accurately, we are more able to discern the precise cause

15
00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.820
of our feelings.

16
00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:23.180
And what scientists call the readiness potential in our brain is activated, allowing us to

17
00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:25.620
take concrete steps.

18
00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:28.700
But not just any steps, the right steps for us.

19
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:31.220
Because our emotions are data.

20
00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.820
Our emotions contain flashing lights to things that we care about.

21
00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:43.380
We tend not to feel strong emotion, to stuff that doesn't mean anything in our worlds.

22
00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:48.780
If you feel rage when you read the news, that rage is a signpost, perhaps, that you value

23
00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.860
equity and fairness.

24
00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:56.260
And an opportunity to take active steps to shape your life in that direction.

25
00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.800
When we are open to the difficulty emotions, we are able to generate responses that are

26
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.060
values aligned.

27
00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.460
But there's an important caveat.

28
00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:07.860
Our emotions are data, they are not directives.

29
00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:13.660
We can show up turn mind our emotions for their values, without needing to listen to them.

30
00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:19.860
Just like I can show up to my son in his frustration with his baby sister.

31
00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:23.740
But not endorse his idea that he gets to give her away to the first stranger he sees in

32
00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.300
a shopping mall.

33
00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:30.700
We own our emotions, they don't own us.

34
00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:35.220
When we internalize the difference between how I feel and all my wisdom and what I do

35
00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:45.580
in a values aligned action, we generate the pathway to our best selves via our emotions.

36
00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:49.620
So what does this look like in practice?

37
00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:54.540
When you feel a strong tough emotion, don't race for the emotional exits.

38
00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:58.820
Learn its contours, show up to the journal of your hearts.

39
00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:02.820
What is the emotion telling you?

40
00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:07.740
And try not to say I am as in I am angry or I am said, when you say I am it makes you

41
00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.260
sound as if you are the emotion.

42
00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:13.740
Whereas you are you and the emotion is a data source.

43
00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:17.540
Instead try to notice the feeling for what it is, I'm noticing that I'm feeling said

44
00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.300
or I'm noticing that I'm feeling angry.
